Rāma moves with Lakṣmaṇa to Prasravaṇa hill cave --- Rāma dwells joyless remembering dearer-than-life wife --- Rāma spends moonlit nights sleepless in grief --- Lakṣmaṇa shares grief urging abandoning sorrow --- Lakṣmaṇa declares Rāma can overturn earth and Rāvaṇa --- Lakṣmaṇa offers waking sleeping valor like ash-covered fire --- Rāma praises loyal Lakṣmaṇa speech abandoning grief --- Rāma rouses valor awaiting rains to kill Rāvaṇa with kin --- Lakṣmaṇa rejoices urging spending rains restraining anger
